      "description": "Advertising & Filling Positions | Human Resources | SFA Skip to main content News Calendar mySFA Search X Can we help you find what you’re looking for? Info For: Future Students Lumberjacks Faculty & Staff Parents High School Counselors Alumni & Friends Division of Organizational Effectiveness Human Resources About HR Policies Organizational Charts (PDF) Staff Prospective Employees About SFA Benefits Overview Prospective Faculty Prospective Staff Faculty & Staff Affordable Care Act Benefits Compensation & Classification Employee Holiday Schedule Employment Verification Employee Wellness Exiting Employment Faculty Resources Leave Lumberjack Education Assistance Program Military Employment Preference Information Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program Managers Advertising & Filling Positions Compensation & Classification EPAF Resources Leave Performance Management Student Internships Volunteers Students Graduate Assistants Student Employment Student Internships Training & Forms Forms Training Axe ’Em, Jacks! Search terms mySFA A-Z About HR Policies Organizational Charts (PDF) Staff Prospective Employees About SFA Benefits Overview Prospective Faculty Prospective Staff Faculty & Staff Affordable Care Act Benefits Compensation & Classification Employee Holiday Schedule Employment Verification Employee Wellness Exiting Employment Faculty Resources Leave Lumberjack Education Assistance Program Military Employment Preference Information Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program Managers Advertising & Filling Positions Compensation & Classification EPAF Resources Leave Performance Management Student Internships Volunteers Students Graduate Assistants Student Employment Student Internships Training & Forms Forms Training Info For Future Students New Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents High School Counselors Alumni & Friends Breadcrumb SFA Human Resources Advertising & Filling Positions Managers Advertising & Filling Positions Compensation & Classification EPAF Resources Leave Performance Management Student Internships Volunteers Advertising Vacant Faculty, Staff and Student Assistant Positions Welcome to SFA's portal for hiring managers, search committee chairs and members! The Hiring Process The hiring process consists of identifying the vacancy and evaluating the need, revising the job description as necessary, selecting a search committee, advertising the vacant position, reviewing and screening applicants, conducting interviews, selecting the successful candidate and finalizing the recruitment process. For a general overview of the hiring process for faculty and staff, see the Hiring Manager Toolkit . Hiring Forms and Resources Applicant Screening Matrix (Excel) Checklist for Recruiting, Interviewing and Hiring (PDF) Search Summary Form (Excel) Search Committee Training Departments are encouraged to schedule search committee training by accessing mySFA and using the myTraining feature or contacting Human Resources. Please note that any SFA employee involved in the screening and/or interview process should be considered a search committee member. For more information, see the Accessing Search Committee Training Through myTraining PDF. Interviewing Resources Interview Evaluation Form (Word Doc) Telephone Screening Interview Questions (PDF) Tips for Conducting the Interview (PDF) Interview Topics to Avoid (PDF) Interview Questions for Faculty (PDF) Interview Questions for Staff (PDF) Checking References Form (PDF) Hiring Adjunct Faculty, Visiting Faculty, Graduate Assistants and Casual Employees Because adjunct faculty, visiting faculty, graduate assistants and casual (short-term or sporadic) positions do not have to be posted, the hiring process differs slightly from what is described above. University departments should complete the following steps: Direct the prospective employee to the Human Resources website to complete the background check consent form. This may be submitted through email, fax, mail or hand-delivered to Human Resources. Complete the appropriate EPAF before the employee starts work. Schedule new hire(s) for Benefits Orientation. Prior to Benefits Orientation, the employee will need to complete the checklist assigned to them in TalentEd Onboard which also includes EEO, Ethics, Safety and Benefits Overview videos. To comply with U.S. law, SFA must verify eligibility for employment for all new employees - within three days of hire - by collecting a Form I-9 and reviewing original documents establishing the employee's eligibility to work in the U.S. Referring to the List of Acceptable Documents , employees may present one identification selection from List A or a combination of one selection from List B and one from List C . The employee will need to bring the original documentation to an authorized representative in Human Resources. Advertising & Filling Positions Compensation & Classification EPAF Resources Leave Performance Management Student Internships Volunteers Create a requisition to request a job posting. NEOED Contact: Human Resources 936.468.2304 Fax: 800.435.3919 hr@sfasu.edu Physical Address: 1936 North Street Austin Building Room 201 Mailing Address: Box 13039 SFA Station Nacogdoches, TX 75962 Can we help you find what you’re looking for? Request Info Visit Contact Us Contact or visit us: 936.468.4SFA (4732) Email Us 1936 North St. Nacogdoches, Texas SFA Homepage Request Info Visit Apply Give Public Course Information and Instructor CVs Faculty and Staff Directory Campus Map Accreditations Licensure and Certification Preparation Programs A-Z List Current Weather Conditions Electronic Accessibility | Nondiscrimination and Title IX | Mental Health Resources | Emergency Management | Complaint Resolution and Report Misconduct | UT System | State of Texas | Statewide Search | Texas Homeland Security | Texas Veterans Portal | Report Fraud, Waste and Abuse | Clery Act Reporting | Institutional Resume | Privacy Notice | Site Policies | We