    "https://www.sfasu.edu/hr/faculty-staff/benefits": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Benefits | Human Resources | SFA Skip to main content News Calendar mySFA Search X Can we help you find what you’re looking for? Info For: Future Students Lumberjacks Faculty & Staff Parents High School Counselors Alumni & Friends Division of Organizational Effectiveness Human Resources About HR Policies Organizational Charts (PDF) Staff Prospective Employees About SFA Benefits Overview Prospective Faculty Prospective Staff Faculty & Staff Affordable Care Act Benefits Compensation & Classification Employee Holiday Schedule Employment Verification Employee Wellness Exiting Employment Faculty Resources Leave Lumberjack Education Assistance Program Military Employment Preference Information Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program Managers Advertising & Filling Positions Compensation & Classification EPAF Resources Leave Performance Management Student Internships Volunteers Students Graduate Assistants Student Employment Student Internships Training & Forms Forms Training Axe ’Em, Jacks! Search terms mySFA A-Z About HR Policies Organizational Charts (PDF) Staff Prospective Employees About SFA Benefits Overview Prospective Faculty Prospective Staff Faculty & Staff Affordable Care Act Benefits Compensation & Classification Employee Holiday Schedule Employment Verification Employee Wellness Exiting Employment Faculty Resources Leave Lumberjack Education Assistance Program Military Employment Preference Information Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program Managers Advertising & Filling Positions Compensation & Classification EPAF Resources Leave Performance Management Student Internships Volunteers Students Graduate Assistants Student Employment Student Internships Training & Forms Forms Training Info For Future Students New Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents High School Counselors Alumni & Friends Breadcrumb SFA Human Resources Benefits Faculty & Staff Affordable Care Act Benefits Annual Enrollment Insurance Retirement Compensation & Classification Employee Holiday Schedule Employment Verification Employee Wellness Exiting Employment Faculty Resources Leave Lumberjack Education Assistance Program Military Employment Preference Information Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program The 2025-26 UT System Benefits for Academic Graduate Student Employees video is available online! More videos are available on the UT Benefits Video Library page. Benefits Stephen F. Austin State University offers eligible SFA employees a high-quality competitive benefits package including: Alternative work schedule and compressed work weeks Employee Assistance Program — Information, advice and support on a wide range of everyday issues, including counseling sessions with a licensed mental health professional, legal and financial resources, and work-life referrals Employee discounts — Includes discounted tickets to athletic and performing arts events, discounted recreation center memberships and retail discounts through the EAP discount purchasing program Employee Wellness program Access to faculty and staff meal plans Faculty and staff recognition — Tenure and exemplary service Insurance — Health, dental, vision, life, accidental death and dismemberment, and short-term and long-term disability, FSA + Dependent Day Care - Flex Accounts, Limeade wellness platform Lumberjack Education Assistance Program Paid time off — Holidays, vacation and sick leave Parent and expectant parent resources Retirement — Teacher Retirement System, optional retirement plan, and contributions to 403B tax-sheltered annuity and 457 deferred compensation plan - pre-tax and after tax Making changes to benefits When can I make changes to my benefits? SFA employees may make changes to their benefits during the following times: Initial hire - 31 days after initial eligibility Summer enrollment Summer enrollment occurs annually, generally during the month of July. An announcement including the dates of summer enrollment is sent to SFA employees via SFA Today and campuswide email. Qualifying life event change Employees have 30 days after one of the following life events to make changes to their benefits: Marriage Divorce Birth or adoption of a child Loss of coverage, employment status change by employee or dependent Can I view or make changes to my benefits online? Yes, by registering your online account through the UT system and making changes to your benefits. Affordable Care Act Benefits Annual Enrollment Insurance Retirement Compensation & Classification Employee Holiday Schedule Employment Verification Employee Wellness Exiting Employment Faculty Resources Leave Lumberjack Education Assistance Program Military Employment Preference Information Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program Internal job opportunities for current SFA employees View positions Contact: Human Resources Benefits 936.468.2304 Fax: 800.435.3919 benefits@sfasu.edu Walk-in Hours Tuesday - Thursday, 9:00 a.m. - 1:00 p.m. 1936 North Street Austin Building Room 201 Can we help you find what you’re looking for? Request Info Visit Contact Us Contact or visit us: 936.468.4SFA (4732) Email Us 1936 North St. Nacogdoches, Texas SFA Homepage Request Info Visit Apply Give Public Course Information and Instructor CVs Faculty and Staff Directory Campus Map Accreditations Licensure and Certification Preparation Programs A-Z List Current Weather Conditions Electronic Accessibility | Nondiscrimination and Title IX | Mental Health Resources | Emergency Management | Complaint Resolution and Report Misconduct | UT System | State of Texas | Statewide Search | Texas Homeland Security | Texas Veterans Portal | Report Fraud, Waste and Abuse | Clery Act Reporting | Institutional Resume | Privacy Notice | Site Policies | Welcome to the DeWitt School of Nursing A top... Visit SFA  SFA Academics Majors, Minors, Degrees, and Online Programs Back To Top SFA on Instagram SFA on YouTube SFA on Twitter SFA on Facebook SFA on LinkedIn more at sfasu.edu/socialmedia About This Si